{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Roots","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity.bwS0_eq_hecke_of_rigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity.bwS0_eq_hecke_of_rigidity","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity.lean#L71-L85","doc":"**The reduction of `bwS0_eq_hecke` (honest, conditional).** Model the gauge row\nand the value map as polynomials `bwPoly`, `valPoly` in the fold parameter.  If both\nhave degree `< s.card` for a finset `s` of fibre points, and they agree on `s` (the\nroot-of-unity agreement `KeystoneLRAmplitudeReal` proves), then they are equal — so\nthe gauge row equals the value map at **every** point, in particular at the\nsubstrate `t₀ = q₀ + q₀⁻¹`.  The residual open content of `bwS0_eq_hecke` is exactly\nthe antecedent: *that the gauge row is such a bounded-degree polynomial* (Habiro\nrigidity), and the finite root agreement — the latter already supplied at the root\nby #4365. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity.eq_of_eval_agree_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity.eq_of_eval_agree_card","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity.lean#L47-L69","doc":"**Interpolation rigidity.** Two polynomials whose degrees are both `< s.card`\nand which agree on a finset `s` of (distinct) points are equal.  A polynomial of\ndegree `< s.card` cannot have the `s.card` roots that their difference would carry\nunless it is zero. ","signatureChunk":0}]}